Step 10 Test

Add Product

curl -X POST http://a5bd3ac80cb3f4eeeb97d7c651cf731e-33221974.ap-southeast-2.elb.amazonaws.com/cart \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d '{"productId":1,"productName":"Laptop","price":50000}'

Giving an error

The actual problem

Your backend pod is not allowed to access DynamoDB.

Step 2: Attach the DynamoDB policy

If you're using the AWS Console:

Go to IAM
Click Roles
Open the role from Step 1 (or the NodeInstanceRole shown in your error)
Click Add permissions
Click Attach policies

Attach:

AmazonDynamoDBFullAccess

Step 3 Restart your pods

$ kubectl rollout restart deployment ecommerce-backend

Wait:

